  "_readme": "HOW TO USE — Each name below is an event. Replace its [] with any number of lines, each shaped like: { \"text\": \"what the line says\", \"url\": \"https://the.link\", \"color\": \"#3E7FC1\" }. \"color\" is optional (any hex code, with or without #; without it the line just uses the pane's text colour). The lines appear inside the event's pop-up pane, in order, each opening in a new tab. Extra tricks: a SECTION name (e.g. \"Temporary farms\") also works as a key — every event in that section without its own lines inherits them — and subtitled Horse Season runs (e.g. \"Horse Season: Yeti\") fall back to the \"Horse Season\" entry. The two events with example entries show how it looks — replace them with real links, then save and refresh the calendar page.",

